Package: rustdaw
Version: 0.7.0
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: RustDAW Project
Depends: libasound2, libpulse0, libgl1
Recommends: ffmpeg
Suggests: fluid-soundfont-gm
Description: Ubuntu-first digital audio workstation
 RustDAW provides mono and stereo recording, low-latency monitoring,
 metronome, timeline editing, session persistence, and stereo export.
 .
 It also imports a song as separated instrument tracks, detects its tempo,
 beat grid and chord chart natively, and plays transcribed MIDI through a
 piano roll editor.
 .
 Instrument tracks play from a SoundFont when one is installed and from a
 built-in General MIDI bank synthesised in Rust when one is not, so nothing
 has to be downloaded for a session to open and sound.
 .
 Song import needs ffmpeg for sample-rate conversion, and a local DSPRO
 Studio worker for the stem separation itself.
